.TH CB 1.SH NAMEcb \- C beautifier.SH SYNOPSIS\fBcb\fR< input.c > output.c.SH DESCRIPTION\fBcb\fRreads C source on the standard input and writes it to the standardoutput laid out one statement to a line, each block indented threespaces deeper than the one around it.  It takes no options and no filenames..nf    int main(){int i;for(i=0;i<3;i++){if(i)printf("%d",i);}return 0;}.ficomes out as.nf    int main(){       int i;       for(i=0;i<3;i++){          if(i)printf("%d",i);       }       return 0;    }.fi.SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOindent, cxref